            "review_title": "Review at Lang Tom Seafood Restaurant",
            "review_text": "Jain\nElektrogorsk, Russia53 contributions\n0\nHighly dissapointed\nAug 2018 • Solo\nI visited LT Seafood today, before asked them on FB page if they accepted credit cards. The answer was positive, so I came in for a dinner. A hostess took me to the table and I looked in the menu. “Grouper” was noticed as market price. What is this market price no one could give the answer. Finally I found out for a 650.000 per fish (market price!!!) Asked for a slipper lobster, but they were out, then for a giant freshwater shrip. Out. And I came at 7:30 pm!!!! Then finally ordered grilled oyster with garlic. Got them in 5 minutes and they were gorgeous. But the time has come for a bill. I told the waiter to pay with a card and he went away. 5 minutes, then 10, I came to the cashier by myself, no one speak even poor English. She didn’t understand what I was asking her to do and started shouting at the waiter. Finally I got the receipt, signed it and then she gave me another one to sign) So I left the restaurant hearing the huge argument between the staff. Highly disappointed of service and my ruined dinner.\nRead more\nWritten August 21, 2018",
